From 4abfeff5f7a7a38050b1cf2cb41fa76e5e9c7b73 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Tupek <mrtupek@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 17 May 2026 16:46:01 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Fix cache indexing in DerivativeSetup and DerivativeApply

Reconcile the per-QP Jacobian cache layout between DerivativeSetup
(which writes the cache) and DerivativeApply (which reads it). The
original code used row-major indexing:

  cache_idx = i * test_op_dim * trial_vdim * total_trial_op_dim
            + k * trial_vdim * total_trial_op_dim
            + j * total_trial_op_dim + (m + m_offset)

This is inconsistent across setup/apply for multi-output integrators
because ik_offset was not tracked across the noutputs loop. Switch to
a column-major layout with an explicit ik_offset accumulator:

  cache_idx = ik_offset
            + i + test_vdim * (k + test_op_dim * (j + trial_vdim * (m + m_offset)))

Also fix DerivativeApply to iterate over all outputs (for_constexpr
over noutputs) rather than hardcoding test_vdim/test_op_dim from
output 0 only. The residual write offset uses an explicit res_offset
accumulator and column-major DOF ordering (i + k * test_vdim) to
match the integration path. The DOF-mapping stage now reshapes from
the correct offset in the residual buffer.

Fixes bugs 1 and 12.
